import Submission.Work.DSMap.Mix2
import Submission.Work.DSM4p.Basic
import Submission.Work.DSM4p.Chart
import Submission.Work.DSM4p.chartLevel_dvd
import Submission.Work.DSM4p.chartLevel_torsionFree

/-!
# DSM4p — the chart tower and what remains of `area_M4p`

This module records the *reduction* of the node `DSMap.Mix2.area_M4p` to two statements about
the chart model of `Submission/Work/DSM4p/Chart.lean`, and proves the parts of the reduction
that are formalisable here.

## What is proved in this area

For a perfectoid `B` (`DSMap.PerfectoidData p B`), a compatible root system `gr` of `g = gr 0`
and the chart levels `D n = chartLevel hgr ϖ n ⊆ B[1/g]` generated by `x_k(n) = ϖ_k^n/g_k`
(so `x_k(n) · gr k = ϖ_k^n` and `x_k(n) = x_{k+1}(n)^p`, with the transition
`x_k(n+1) = ϖ_k · x_k(n)`), the following are proved:

* `chartLevel_torsionFree` — every level is `p`-torsion-free (`p` a nonzerodivisor), since it
  is a subring of the localisation `B[1/g]` of a `p`-torsion-free ring;
* `chartLevel_dvd` — the divisibility clause `∃ y, g · y = p^n` of the node holds at every
  level (this is the only place `PerfectoidData.unit`, `ϖ_0^p = p·v`, is used);
* `chartTower_cokernel` — the **cokernel clause** of `IsQRETp` for the chart tower, with the
  uniform constant `c = p^{k+1}·m` (`p^{k+1}` rather than Bhatt's `p^k` because the node's
  clause is modulo `p^m` where Bhatt's is modulo `t^m` and `p = ϖ_0^p · unit`): for every
  `y` in level `n+c`, the element `ϖ_k g_k · y` is congruent modulo `p^m · D n` to an element
  of `B`.  This is Bhatt's Theorem 3.1(2), whose two-case computation (arXiv:1608.08882,
  proof of Theorem 3.1) is `Work.DSM4p.chartMono_estimate` and is delegated/proved in this
  directory.

## What remains (the two gaps)

1. **Perfectoidness of the levels.** The chart levels are the *algebraic skeleton* of the
   Riemann extension tower: the actual levels of the node are the `ϖ`-adic completions
   `B⟨ϖ_0^{pn}/g⟩` of (the ideals of definition of) these rings, and Scholze's Lemma 6.4
   (`ScholzePerfectoidSpaces`) identifies the two modulo `p^m`; the completions carry the
   `PerfectoidData` structure (`ϖ`-compatible, `p`-torsion-free, `p`-adically complete,
   Frobenius invertible mod `ϖ`), while the algebraic skeleton does not (it is not complete).
   Formalising this requires the theory of rational localisations of perfectoid algebras.
   *Note also (a correction to a naive presentation):* the quotient
   `B[x_k]/(x_k g_k = ϖ_k^n, x_{k+1}^p = x_k)` is **not** `p`-torsion-free in general — for
   `gr k = ϖ_k`, `n = 1` the relations give `ϖ_0(x_0 - 1) = 0`, whence `p(x_0 - 1) =
   ϖ_0^{p-1}·ϖ_0(x_0-1) = 0` — so the model has to be the localisation `B[1/g]`, as here, and
   the levels of the node have to be completions of *subrings of `B[1/g]`*.
2. **The kernel clause.** For `x ∈ B` whose image in level `n+c` is divisible by `p^m` one
   must have `ϖ_k g_k x ∈ p^m B` (uniformly in `n`).  This is Bhatt's Theorem 3.1(1) together
   with the base-change argument of Remark 3.2 (which is what allows the hypothesis "`g` is a
   nonzerodivisor modulo `t^m`" to be dropped); it is not `p`-torsion or divisibility
   bookkeeping, and it is not proved here.  It is packaged below as `ChartKernel`.

## Contents

* `Work.DSM4p.retC` — the uniform constant `c = p^{k+1}·m`;
* `Work.DSM4p.chartIterTr_coe` — the iterated transition of the chart tower is the coercion
  into `B[1/g]` (the transitions are the inclusions of levels);
* `Work.DSM4p.ChartKernel`, `Work.DSM4p.ChartCokernel` — the two clauses of `IsQRETAt` for the
  chart tower, at the constant `retC`;
* `Work.DSM4p.isQRETAt_chartTower` — `ChartKernel → ChartCokernel → IsQRETAt …` for the chart
  tower: the reduction, with the kernel clause isolated as the single unproved input of the
  chart model.

The cokernel clause is proved (`Work.DSM4p.chartCokernel`, at the constant `retC`); see
`Submission/Work/DSM4p/Assembly.lean`, `Submission/Work/DSM4p/chartComp_isQRETp.lean` and
`Submission/Work/DSM4p/areaM4p_of_kernel.lean` for the transfer to the completed levels and the
resulting reduction of the node to `ChartKernel ∧ frobInj`.
-/

set_option linter.style.haveILetI false

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Limits

namespace Work.DSM4p

universe a

open DSMap DSMap.Mix DSMap.Mix2

/-- The uniform constant of the pro form: `c = p^(k+1) · m`.  (Bhatt's Theorem 3.1 uses
`c = p^k · m` with clauses modulo `t^m`; here the clauses are modulo `p^m` and `p = ϖ_0^p` up
to a unit, which is the `p^(k+1)`.) -/
def retC (p k m : ℕ) : ℕ := p ^ (k + 1) * m

section ChartTower

variable {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] {B : Type a} [CommRing B]
variable (Q : PerfectoidData p B) (gr : ℕ → B) (hgr : IsRootSystem p gr)

/-- The iterated transition of the chart tower is the coercion into `B[1/g]`: the transitions
`chartTr` are the inclusions of the levels. -/
theorem chartIterTr_coe (n c : ℕ) (y : chartRing hgr Q.ϖ (n + c)) :
    (iterTr (chartTr hgr Q.ϖ) n c y : ChartAmbient gr) = (y : ChartAmbient gr) := by
  induction c with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ c ih => rw [iterTr_succ]; exact ih (chartTr hgr Q.ϖ (n + c) y)

/-- The cokernel clause of `IsQRETAt` for the chart tower, at the constant `retC p k m`:
every element of level `n + retC` is, up to `p^m` in level `n`, equal to an element of `B`
after multiplication by `ϖ_k g_k`. -/
def ChartCokernel (m k : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (y : chartRing hgr Q.ϖ (n + retC p k m)), ∃ x : B,
    algebraMap B (chartRing hgr Q.ϖ n) (Q.ϖ k * gr k) *
        iterTr (chartTr hgr Q.ϖ) n (retC p k m) y -
      algebraMap B (chartRing hgr Q.ϖ n) x ∈
        Ideal.span {((p : chartRing hgr Q.ϖ n)) ^ m}

/-- The kernel clause of `IsQRETAt` for the chart tower, at the constant `retC p k m`.  This
is the *only* clause of the node that is not established in this area (see the module
docstring): it is Bhatt's Theorem 3.1(1) with the uniform base-change argument of Remark
3.2. -/
def ChartKernel (m k : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (x : B),
    algebraMap B (chartRing hgr Q.ϖ (n + retC p k m)) x ∈
        Ideal.span {((p : chartRing hgr Q.ϖ (n + retC p k m))) ^ m} →
      Q.ϖ k * gr k * x ∈ Ideal.span {((p : B)) ^ m}

/-- The two clauses at the uniform constant `retC p k m` give the QRET condition at level
`(m, k)` for the chart tower. -/
theorem isQRETAt_chartTower (m k : ℕ) (hk : ChartKernel Q gr hgr m k)
    (hc : ChartCokernel Q gr hgr m k) :
    IsQRETAt p B Q.ϖ gr (chartRing hgr Q.ϖ) (chartTr hgr Q.ϖ) m k :=
  ⟨retC p k m, hk, hc⟩

/-- `IsQRETp` for the chart tower, from the kernel clause at every level.  (The cokernel
clause is `Work.DSM4p.chartTower_cokernel`; the chart model still has to be replaced by the
completed perfectoid levels, see the module docstring.) -/
theorem isQRETp_chartTower (hk : ∀ m k, ChartKernel Q gr hgr m k)
    (hc : ∀ m k, ChartCokernel Q gr hgr m k) :
    IsQRETp p B Q.ϖ gr (chartRing hgr Q.ϖ) (chartTr hgr Q.ϖ) :=
  fun m k => isQRETAt_chartTower Q gr hgr m k (hk m k) (hc m k)

end ChartTower

end Work.DSM4p
